# Testing & Quality Rules

## Test pyramid
Prefer fast domain/unit tests, then application tests, API/contract tests, integration/provider tests and a smaller set of end-to-end tests.

## Mandatory high-risk coverage
Maintain automated tests for:
- tenant isolation and cross-tenant denial;
- RBAC and sensitive permissions;
- all important state-machine transitions and invalid transitions;
- commission calculation and snapshotting;
- 15-day hold and availability;
- refund/chargeback reversal;
- payout atomic reservation and race conditions;
- payment webhook idempotency and replay;
- phone reservation/purchase reconciliation;
- webhook signing, verification, retries and replay;
- agent publish preflight and tool allowlist;
- knowledge-scope isolation;
- customer-risk/chargeback agent shutdown;
- critical call routing and lifecycle.

## Contract testing
External contracts must have explicit schemas and tests. Test both happy path and malformed/duplicate/out-of-order provider events.

## Regression discipline
When modifying billing, commission, KYC, payouts, tenancy, permissions, call routing or customer data, run the affected regression suite before completion.

## Static quality
Use formatter, linter, type checking and dependency/security scanning appropriate to the actual package. Do not weaken checks to make CI green.

## Definition of done
A feature is not complete because the code runs. It is complete only when requirements, authorization, failure behavior, observability, tests and documentation are addressed.

## Release gate
Do not recommend production release if critical tests fail, tenant isolation is unverified, financial idempotency is missing, backups have not been restore-tested, or critical observability/alerts are absent.
